        "{\"event\":{\"at\":\"2026-11-03T21:11:26.417Z\",\"kind\":\"decision.recorded\",\"payload\":{\"adr\":\"ADR-2\",\"alternatives\":\"`\\\\s+` after `export`: turned down, JS `\\\\s` matches Unicode whitespace (NBSP and others) and PHP `\\\\s` without /u does not, so the two packages would disagree on the same input. Strip the prefix only after the comment check: turned down, `export #X=1` would then define a key named `#X`, unlike `#X=1`, which is a comment. Match a literal `export ` (one space) only: turned down, `export\\\\tKEY=v` would keep the key `export\\\\tKEY`. Accept `export` with no following whitespace: turned down, it would swallow a key that is really named `export`.\",\"rationale\":\"`export KEY=value` is a shell habit, so a line written that way is read exactly as `KEY=value`. The prefix is removed from the trimmed line before the blank/comment check, so `export # note` is a comment and `export NOVALUE` is skipped, as if the prefix were absent. It applies once, so `export export=1` has the key `export`. The prefix needs at least one space or tab after `export`, so `export=kept` and `exportKEY=y` keep their own keys. Made in both `packages/js` and `packages/php` in the same change, as ADR-1 requires. The match is the ASCII class `[ \\\\t]+` in both.\",\"title\":\"EnvAccessor drops a leading `export` followed by spaces or tabs, in both packages\"},\"run\":\"01a1a340-58d9-7000-8b73-254e5b919c3a\",\"signerFp\":\"2c0b8f36a867ee3d0d75bcb569c7e57d47032f1b1ea022d9f875f7b762c5d58a\",\"subject\":\"01a1a340-a9c5-7000-ada8-9adf034b70f5\",\"v\":1,\"which\":\"claude-code\",\"who\":\"mnid:65336f82ebe4c7cf5737f0e96b8df5aa61e2422fa8e9ac64d90b7f6607eb8c4a\"},\"link\":{\"hash\":\"7321db54844cfe88b4c9853d8f08d4f755b10d822457d854b7078ba776b340b4\",\"prev\":\"bd8aa8ab2af1ea4865e395fa459f598e67af852693077901fac97d101b098528\",\"seq\":3,\"tail\":\"2c0b8f36a867ee3d0d75bcb569c7e57d47032f1b1ea022d9f875f7b762c5d58a-b378dc95dd8ef29761ebdd0c5717c86f\"}}",
